## Prerequisites

- Terraform 1.3 or newer
- Google Cloud CLI (`gcloud`)
- The Compute Engine API enabled in `{{project_id}}`{{#if enable_private_link}}, plus the Cloud DNS API{{/if}}
- The caller granted `roles/iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator` on `{{google_service_account_email}}`
- `{{google_service_account_email}}` with project permissions required to {{#if create_new_vpc}}create the VPC, subnets,{{#if enable_private_link}} PSC endpoints, DNS,{{/if}} networking resources, and Databricks workspace{{else}}{{#if enable_private_link}}create the PSC subnet, endpoints, private DNS zones,{{#if enable_nat_gateway}} Cloud Router, Cloud NAT,{{/if}} and read the existing VPC and subnet in `{{vpc_network_project_id}}`, plus create the Databricks workspace{{else}}create the Databricks workspace and read the existing VPC and subnet{{/if}}{{/if}}
{{#unless create_new_vpc}}
{{#if enable_private_link}}
{{#unless (eq vpc_network_project_id project_id)}}
- The Compute Engine and Cloud DNS APIs also enabled in the VPC host project `{{vpc_network_project_id}}`, where the PSC subnet, endpoints, and DNS zones are created
{{/unless}}
{{#if enable_nat_gateway}}
- No existing Cloud NAT gateway in `{{region}}` on `{{vpc_name}}`. The generated Cloud NAT serves every subnet in the region and can conflict with an existing gateway; set `create_nat_gateway = false` in `terraform.tfvars` if one is already present
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{/unless}}
- The same service account added to the Databricks account and assigned the Account Admin role
- `{{databricks_admin_user}}` already present as a Databricks account user

