## Authenticate

Configure the project and impersonate the service account used by both Terraform providers. See [service account impersonation](https://cloud.google.com/docs/authentication/use-service-account-impersonation).

```bash
gcloud config set project {{project_id}}
gcloud config set auth/impersonate_service_account {{google_service_account_email}}
export GOOGLE_OAUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN="$(gcloud auth print-access-token)"
```

The access token is intentionally not stored in `terraform.tfvars`. Refresh it if Terraform reports that it has expired.

## Deploy

```bash
terraform init
terraform validate
terraform plan
terraform apply
```

After deployment:

```bash
terraform output -raw workspace_url
```

## Resources created

{{#if enable_private_link}}
{{#if create_new_vpc}}
The deployment creates a VPC, node and PSC subnets with Private Google Access, two Back-end PSC endpoints, private DNS records, a Databricks MWS network and private access settings, a workspace, Unity Catalog metastore assignment, and workspace admin membership. {{#if enable_nat_gateway}}Cloud Router and Cloud NAT provide general outbound connectivity.{{else}}Cloud NAT is disabled, so workloads need an alternate route for general internet egress.{{/if}}
{{else}}
The deployment reuses the existing VPC and node subnet, then creates a dedicated PSC subnet, two Back-end PSC endpoints, private DNS records, a Databricks MWS network and private access settings, a workspace, Unity Catalog metastore assignment, and workspace admin membership. {{#if enable_nat_gateway}}Cloud Router and Cloud NAT provide general outbound connectivity.{{else}}Cloud NAT is disabled, so workloads need an alternate route for general internet egress.{{/if}}
{{/if}}

The PSC service attachments are selected for `{{region}}`; confirm current regional values in the [Databricks regional infrastructure documentation](https://docs.databricks.com/gcp/en/resources/ip-domain-region#psc) before deployment.
{{else}}{{#if create_new_vpc}}
The deployment creates a VPC, a subnet with Private Google Access, Cloud Router, Cloud NAT, a Databricks MWS network, a workspace, a Unity Catalog metastore (or assignment to an existing metastore), and workspace admin membership. Databricks creates the workspace cloud-storage buckets.
{{else}}
The deployment creates a Databricks MWS network that references the existing VPC and subnet, a workspace, a Unity Catalog metastore (or assignment to an existing metastore), and workspace admin membership. The existing VPC and subnet are not modified.
{{/if}}{{/if}}

## Destroy

```bash
terraform destroy
```

If the VPC remains in use by Databricks-managed firewall rules, complete the Databricks workspace teardown before retrying. An existing metastore attached by ID is not destroyed.

